DA:Teduglutida is a pharmacological analog of GLP-2 used for treating short bowel syndrome (SIC) in patients aged 1 year or older.OCTREOTIDO:Octreotide is a medication recommended for short-term use in patients with terminal jejunostomy and high output.ADENOMAS DE COLON:Colon adenomas are benign tumors that can develop in the colon, which may increase in number and size with certain treatments.TRASPLANTE INTESTINAL:El trasplante intestinal es un procedimiento quir√∫rgico que se ha establecido como una opci√≥n de tratamiento para pacientes que sufren de fallo intestinal cr√≥nico. Este procedimiento permite la restauraci√≥n de la funci√≥n intestinal, lo que es crucial para la salud y el bienestar de los pacientes. Est√° indicado especialmente en aquellos que presentan complicaciones graves relacionadas con la nutrici√≥n parenteral, as√≠ como en casos de fallo intestinal severo que amenazan la vida.ENFERMEDAD HEP√ÅTICA ASOCIADA A FALLA INTESTINAL:La enfermedad hep√°tica asociada a fallo intestinal (EHAFI) es una complicaci√≥n que puede surgir en pacientes con s√≠ndrome de intestino corto, manifest√°ndose como colestasis o esteatosis hep√°tica.FLUIDOS INTRAVENOSOS:Los fluidos intravenosos son soluciones administradas a trav√©s de una vena para tratar la deshidrataci√≥n y mantener la hidrataci√≥n en pacientes, especialmente aquellos con condiciones cr√≠ticas como el s√≠ndrome de intestino corto.TROMBOSIS VENOSA CENTRAL:La trombosis venosa central es una complicaci√≥n que puede ocurrir en pacientes que reciben nutrici√≥n parenteral, afectando su tratamiento y salud general.DESHIDRATACI√ìN SEVERA:La deshidrataci√≥n severa es una condici√≥n que puede presentarse en pacientes con s√≠ndrome de intestino corto, a pesar de la administraci√≥n de fluidos intravenosos y nutrici√≥n parenteral.S√çNDROME DE INTESTINO ULTRACORTO:El s√≠ndrome de intestino ultracorto es una condici√≥n cr√≠tica que puede llevar a la necesidad de trasplante intestinal en pacientes con fallo intestinal cr√≥nico.EHAFI:EHAFI refers to a condition that requires specific prophylactic measures to be applied in patients, particularly in the context of nutritional support and lipid administration.DAPTOMICINA:Daptomicina is an antibiotic that is effective against biofilms formed on central venous catheters and is used in the treatment of infections related to these catheters.NPD:NPD, which stands for Nutrici√≥n Parenteral Domiciliaria, refers to a type of nutritional support provided at home, specifically regulated under the Spanish healthcare system. This method of nutritional support is particularly utilized for patients with intestinal failure, employing Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) to meet their dietary needs.ACIDOSIS D-L√ÅCTICA:Acidosis D-l√°ctica is a significant complication in patients with SIC, resulting from the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates by Lactobacillus.CAT√âTER VENOSO CENTRAL:The "CAT√âTER VENOSO CENTRAL" is a medical device designed for intravenous access in patients, facilitating the administration of treatments and medications. It is particularly essential for delivering high-osmolarity parenteral nutrition. However, the use of central venous catheters is not without risks, as they can lead to complications such as infections and thrombosis. Overall, while the central venous catheter serves a critical role in patient care, healthcare providers must be vigilant about the potential complications associated with its use.FISTULA ARTERIOVENOSA:An arteriovenous fistula may be beneficial for some patients for the administration of NPD, providing an alternative access route.F√çSTULA ARTERIOVENOSA:A surgical procedure used for the administration of NPD3, potentially beneficial for some patients.SUSRUTA:An ancient Indian physician known as the father of medicine, who described treatments for entero-cutaneous fistulas in his work Susrutasamhit.ANTICOAGULANTES:Medications used to treat venous thrombosis, varying in duration based on individual patient needs.SOLUCI√ìN SALINA:A saline solution recommended for flushing catheters to prevent obstruction and maintain patency.F√ÅRMACOS FIBRINOL√çTICOS:Medications used to attempt to dissolve clots in cases where saline solution fails to clear catheter obstructions.DRENAJES:Medical devices used to remove fluids from the body, which require careful monitoring in patients with FEC.ALTERACIONES NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional imbalances that are common in patients with FEC, contributing to morbidity and mortality.SUCRALFATO:Sucralfate is a medication primarily used to treat ulcers and is included in the treatment options for patients undergoing FEC (chemotherapy regimen). It is important to administer sucralfate with caution, particularly when used in conjunction with enteral nutrition, as it can lead to complications such as obstruction of feeding tubes. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, sucralfate should be taken with meals. Overall, while sucralfate is effective for ulcer treatment, careful consideration is necessary when integrating it into the care of patients receiving enteral nutrition.OCTRE√ìTIDO:A medication used in the management of high-output fistulas, included in the treatment options for patients with FEC.D√âBITO:The output or flow rate from a fistula, which influences nutritional management decisions.DIETA POBRE EN RESIDUOS:A dietary approach recommended for patients with certain gastrointestinal conditions, aimed at reducing stool output.SOLUCI√ìN DE REHIDRATACI√ìN ORAL ISOT√ìNICA:An oral rehydration solution recommended for patients with high output from fistulas.FISTULACLISIS:A technique used to maintain nutritional status in patients with fistulas by using the fistulous opening for feeding.DILATACI√ìN INTESTINAL:La dilataci√≥n intestinal difusa puede ocurrir en pacientes con POIC, requiriendo drenaje mediante ostom√≠as.DIAMOND S:Diamond S is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing intestinal failure and its clinical implications.HURT RT:Hurt RT is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing intestinal failure and its clinical implications.MARTINDALE R:Martindale R is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing intestinal failure and its clinical implications.PIRONI L:Pironi L is an author recognized for significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to chronic nutrition, as evidenced by their involvement in the ESPEN guidelines. Additionally, Pironi L has co-authored bibliographic references that address the definitions of intestinal failure and short bowel syndrome, further highlighting their expertise and influence in these medical areas.ARRENDS J:Arends J is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing guidelines on chronic intestinal failure in adults.BOZZETTI F:Bozzetti F is a prominent researcher and author recognized for significant contributions to the field of nutritional support, particularly in the context of cancer patients. He has been actively involved in research focusing on artificial nutritional support and its clinical applications. Bozzetti F has also played a crucial role in developing the ESPEN guidelines on chronic nutrition, as well as guidelines specifically addressing enteral nutrition in oncology. Additionally, he is one of the authors of bibliographic references that discuss guidelines on chronic intestinal failure in adults, further highlighting his expertise and influence in the area of nutritional care for patients with complex medical needs.CUERDA C:Cuerda C is a prominent member of the NADYA group, where they play a significant role in contributing to reports on home parenteral nutrition in Spain. As a dedicated researcher, Cuerda C focuses on studies related to health-related quality of life for patients receiving home nutritional support. Additionally, Cuerda C is an author involved in the development of the ESPEN guidelines on chronic nutrition, further showcasing their expertise in the field. They are also recognized for their contributions to bibliographic references that discuss guidelines on chronic intestinal failure in adults, highlighting their commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in nutritional support.GILLANDERS L:Gillanders L is an author recognized for their contributions to the ESPEN guidelines on chronic nutrition. Additionally, Gillanders L is noted as one of the authors of bibliographic references that discuss guidelines on chronic intestinal failure in adults. This involvement highlights Gillanders L's expertise and commitment to advancing knowledge in the field of nutrition and intestinal health.JEPPESEN PB:Jeppesen PB is an author who has contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on chronic nutrition. Additionally, Jeppesen PB is recognized as one of the authors of bibliographic references that discuss guidelines specifically related to chronic intestinal failure in adults.GARDINER KR:Gardiner KR is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing management of acute intestinal failure.CARROLL RE:Carroll RE is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing management and complications of short bowel syndrome.BENEDICTI E:Benedicti E is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing management and complications of short bowel syndrome.SCHOWALTER JP:Schowalter JP is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing management and complications of short bowel syndrome.BUCHMAN AL:Buchman AL is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing management and complications of short bowel syndrome.WEALE AR:Weale AR is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing intestinal adaptation after massive intestinal resection.EDWARDS AG:Edwards AG is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing intestinal adaptation after massive intestinal resection.BAILEY M:Bailey M is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing intestinal adaptation after massive intestinal resection.LEAR PA:Lear PA is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing intestinal adaptation after massive intestinal resection.JUANA-ROA J:Juana-Roa J is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing the reality of home parenteral nutrition in Spain.LOZANO CWB:Lozano CWB is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing the reality of home parenteral nutrition in Spain.SANZ-VALERO J:Sanz-Valero J is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing the reality of home parenteral nutrition in Spain.POLK TM:Polk TM is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing metabolic and nutritional support of the enterocutaneous fistula patient.SCHWAB CW:Schwab CW is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing metabolic and nutritional support of the enterocutaneous fistula patient.BILLIAUWS L:Billiauws L is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing dysmotility disorders and nutritional approaches.CORCOS O:Corcos O is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing dysmotility disorders and nutritional approaches.JOLY F:Joly F is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing nutritional support in severely compromised motility patients.LAMPRECHT G:Lamprecht G is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing nutritional strategies to enhance adaptation in intestinal failure.DAVIDSON J:Davidson J is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing adult intestinal failure.PLUMB A:Plumb A is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing adult intestinal failure.BURNETT H:Burnett H is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing adult intestinal failure.LAPPAS JC:Lappas JC is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing imaging of the postsurgical small bowel.CRENN P:Crenn P is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing citrulline as a biomarker of intestinal failure.MESSING B:Messing B is an author who specializes in the study of catheter infection prevention during parenteral nutrition. Additionally, Messing B has contributed to bibliographic references that focus on nutritional support for patients with severely compromised motility.CYNOBER L:Cynober L is an author engaged in research focused on glutamine supplementation for critically ill patients. Additionally, Cynober L has contributed to bibliographic references that explore the use of citrulline as a biomarker for intestinal failure.DIBAIS JK:DiBaise JK is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing enteral access options and management in patients with intestinal failure.DECKER GA:Decker GA is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing enteral access options and management in patients with intestinal failure.ALFARO JJ:Alfaro JJ is one of the authors of the bibliographic references discussing refeeding syndrome in ICU patients.)<|COMPLETE|>ANTONIO HERN√ÅNDEZ L√ìPEZ:Antonio Hern√°ndez L√≥pez is a medical professional associated with the field of endocrinology and nutrition at the Complejo Hospitalario Universitario in Albacete.JOS√â JOAQU√çN ALFARO MART√çNEZ:Jos√© Joaqu√≠n Alfaro Mart√≠nez is a medical professional involved in nutrition and diet therapy, contributing to the field of clinical nutrition.COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO:The Complejo Hospitalario Universitario in Albacete is a healthcare institution where various medical professionals, including those specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, work.REVESTIVE:Revestive is a medication developed by Shire Pharmaceuticals used for the treatment of short bowel syndrome and related conditions.SURGICAL MANAGEMENT OF SHORT BOWEL SYNDROME:A medical procedure or study focusing on the surgical approaches to managing short bowel syndrome, highlighting various techniques and outcomes.CURRENT OPINION IN ORGAN TRANSPLANTATION:A publication that discusses the latest developments and opinions regarding organ transplantation, including surgical therapies for intestinal failure.CIRUG√çA PEDI√ÅTRICA:A journal that publishes research and findings related to pediatric surgery, including nutritional management in surgical patients.AMERICAN JOURNAL OF HEALTH SYSTEM PHARMACY:A publication that provides insights into health system pharmacy practices, including studies on drug stability and compatibility.SURGICAL CLINICS OF NORTH AMERICA:A journal that publishes articles on various surgical practices and controversies, including the management of enterocutaneous fistulas.NUTRICI√ìN HOSPITALARIA: √ìRGANO OFICIAL DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL:An official journal of the Spanish Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition, focusing on clinical nutrition topics.CIRUG√çA PEDI√ÅTRICA: √ìRGANO OFICIAL DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE CIRUG√çA PEDI√ÅTRICA:An official journal of the Spanish Society of Pediatric Surgery, discussing various aspects of pediatric surgical care.SHIRE PHARMACEUTICALS IRELAND LIMITED:ENHANCED RECOVERY AFTER SURGERY:Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) is a program established to improve recovery for patients undergoing elective surgery through multimodal rehabilitation protocols.KEHLET:Kehlet is a medical professional who proposed new strategies for perioperative management to reduce surgical stress and improve recovery in 1997.SCOTLAND:Scotland is one of the five northern European countries that contributed to the establishment of the ERAS group.NORWAY:Norway is a significant contributor to international health and research initiatives. It provided data for the World Health Organization's (WHO) international growth reference patterns for children, aiding in the establishment of global health standards. Additionally, Norway is one of the five northern European countries that played a crucial role in the formation of the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) group, which focuses on improving surgical recovery protocols. Through these contributions, Norway demonstrates its commitment to advancing health and medical practices on an international scale.NETHERLANDS:The Netherlands is one of the five northern European countries that contributed to the establishment of the ERAS group.MULTIMODAL REHABILITATION:Multimodal rehabilitation refers to the combination of various interventions aimed at improving recovery outcomes for patients undergoing surgery.PERIOPERATIVE CARE:Perioperative care encompasses the care provided before, during, and after surgery, which is crucial for patient recovery.FAST-TRACK SURGERY:Fast-track surgery is a term used to describe surgical protocols designed to expedite recovery and reduce hospital stay.DUODENOPANCREATECTOMY:Duodenopancreatectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of both the duodenum and the pancreas. This procedure is often discussed in the context of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols, which aim to improve recovery outcomes for patients. Additionally, duodenopancreatectomy necessitates careful nutritional management to support the patient's recovery and overall health following the surgery.RECTAL SURGERY:Rectal surgery encompasses surgical procedures performed on the rectum, which may incorporate Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols to enhance patient outcomes. These protocols are designed to optimize recovery and improve overall surgical results, making rectal surgery a critical component of modern surgical practices.MORBIDITY:Morbidity refers to the condition of being diseased or the incidence of illness, encompassing the presence of disease or medical conditions that affect health and quality of life. It is a critical focus for initiatives like Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS), which aims to reduce morbidity through improved surgical protocols.ERAS:ERAS, which stands for Enhanced Recovery After Surgery, is a comprehensive set of recommendations designed to enhance the recovery process for patients following surgical procedures. Initially published in 2005 and updated in subsequent years, ERAS serves as a multimodal protocol specifically for elective colon surgery. The protocol focuses on improving patient outcomes by implementing various perioperative care strategies that facilitate a smoother and more efficient recovery.NUTRITION RISK SCREENING:Nutrition Risk Screening (NRS-2002) is one of the tools used to assess nutritional risk in patients undergoing major scheduled surgery.MST:Malnutrition Screening Tool (MST) is a simple tool used to identify malnutrition in various patient populations.NRI:The Nutrition Risk Index (NRI) is a method utilized to evaluate the nutritional status of patients. It serves as a scoring system that assesses the nutritional risk of individuals primarily based on their albumin levels and weight. This index is instrumental in identifying patients who may be at risk of malnutrition, thereby facilitating timely interventions to improve their nutritional health.MULTIDISCIPLINARY INTEGRATION:Multidisciplinary integration involves collaboration among various healthcare professionals, which is essential for the successful implementation of ERAS protocols.POSTOPERATIVE COMPLICATIONS:Postoperative complications refer to adverse effects that can arise following surgical procedures. These complications can be influenced by various factors, including a patient's nutritional status and changes in body composition resulting from cancer treatment. Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols are designed to mitigate these complications by providing improved nutritional support and comprehensive care, thereby promoting better recovery outcomes for patients.HOSPITAL STAY:Hospital stay refers to the duration a patient remains in the hospital following surgery. This duration can be influenced by various factors, including the patient's nutritional status and the implementation of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols. Additionally, nutritional support and interventions play a significant role in determining the length of time a patient spends in the hospital.READMISSION RATES:Readmission rates refer to the frequency of patients returning to the hospital after discharge, which can be affected by nutritional support and surgical protocols.COLON SURGERY:CANCER G√ÅSTRICO:Gastric cancer, a condition for which various nutritional screening methods have been comparedPAR√ÅMETROS ANTROPOM√âTRICOS:Measurements of the human body used to assess nutritional status, which have limitations in predicting surgical complicationsPAR√ÅMETROS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional indicators such as albumin levels that are used in nutritional screeningVALORACI√ìN DE LA FUERZA MUSCULAR:An assessment of muscle strength that can be part of nutritional screening but has limited predictive value for surgical complicationsGRAVEDAD DE LA ENFERMEDAD:The severity of underlying health conditions that can affect nutritional status and surgical outcomesNUTRICIONAL RISK INDEX:SURGERY:Surgery is a medical procedure commonly utilized in the treatment of esophageal cancer. It plays a crucial role in managing the disease, but it also significantly impacts the nutritional status of patients. This impact can lead to complications, particularly in those who are malnourished. Therefore, careful management of nutrition and body composition is essential both before and after the operation to ensure optimal patient outcomes. Studies have highlighted the importance of nutritional support in the postoperative recovery of cancer patients undergoing surgery, emphasizing that such support may be necessary to mitigate potential complications and enhance recovery. Overall, surgery is a vital medical service that requires comprehensive care, including attention to the nutritional needs of patients.AYUNO PREOPERATORIO:AYUNO PREOPERATORIO refers to the practice of fasting prior to surgical procedures, which has been developed and refined over time to minimize the risk of complications during surgery. This preoperative fasting is recommended to ensure patient safety and improve surgical outcomes by preventing issues such as aspiration and other related complications.ANESTESIA:Anesthesia is a medical intervention used during surgery to prevent pain and awareness, influencing preoperative fasting guidelines.CIRUG√çA GASTROINTESTINAL:CIRUG√çA GASTROINTESTINAL refers to surgical procedures performed on the gastrointestinal tract. These procedures may necessitate nutritional support both before and after the surgery, ensuring that patients receive the necessary care to aid in their recovery.SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL POSTOPERATORIO:SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL POSTOPERATORIO refers to the nutritional support provided to patients after surgery to aid recovery.√çLEO POSTOPERATORIO:√çLEO POSTOPERATORIO refers to a condition that can occur after surgery, characterized by a temporary cessation of bowel activity.PEY:PEY refers to jejunostomy, a surgical procedure to create an opening in the jejunum for feeding.PROCEDIMIENTO QUIR√öRGICO:PROCEDIMIENTO QUIR√öRGICO refers to surgical procedures that may require nutritional support before and after.REHABILITACI√ìN MULTIMODAL:REHABILITACI√ìN MULTIMODAL refers to a comprehensive set of post-surgical interventions designed to accelerate recovery and minimize complications following surgery. This approach incorporates various protocols, including early postoperative feeding, which is specifically aimed at enhancing the recovery process for patients.INMUNOGLOBULINA A:INMUNOGLOBULINA A is an antibody that plays a crucial role in the immune function of the intestinal mucosa.TROFISMO DE LA MUCOSA INTESTINAL:TROFISMO DE LA MUCOSA INTESTINAL refers to the health and integrity of the intestinal lining, which can be affected by nutritional support.YEYUNOSTOM√çA ENDOSC√ìPICA PERCUT√ÅNEA:A surgical procedure for providing enteral nutrition through the jejunum using an endoscope.PROTOCOLOS ERAS:Enhanced Recovery After Surgery protocols designed to improve recovery outcomes for surgical patients.FISTULAS DE ALTO D√âBITO:FISTULAS DE ALTO D√âBITO are medical conditions that may necessitate specialized nutritional support due to high output.OBSTRUCCI√ìN DIGESTIVA PARCIAL:OBSTRUCCI√ìN DIGESTIVA PARCIAL is a condition that can affect nutrient absorption and may require nutritional intervention.GUIDELINES:GUIDELINES are systematic recommendations established by ASPEN to provide nutritional support for surgical patients. These guidelines serve as protocols aimed at improving patient care and outcomes, particularly focusing on the prevention of complications in transplant recipients. They are designed to assist healthcare professionals in making informed decisions about patient care based on evidence, ensuring that the best practices are followed in various clinical settings.KEHLET H:Kehlet H is a researcher known for his work on multimodal approaches to control postoperative pathophysiology and rehabilitation.MORTENSEN K:Mortensen K is a researcher involved in the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) Group guidelines.SCHIESSER M:INTERNATIONAL CONSENSUS GUIDELINE COMMITTEE:The International Consensus Guideline Committee is a group that proposes guidelines for the diagnosis of malnutrition in clinical practice settings.NATIONAL ALLIANCE FOR INFUSION THERAPY:The National Alliance for Infusion Therapy is an organization that addresses issues related to infusion therapy and malnutrition.NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING (NRS-2002):Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS-2002) is a method based on controlled clinical trials for assessing nutritional risk.RYU SW:Ryu SW is a researcher known for his contributions to the field of nutritional assessments, particularly in the context of gastric cancer patients. He is the author of a study that compares various nutritional assessment methods to detect malnutrition among these patients, which was published in the World Journal of Gastroenterology. Through his work, Ryu SW has played a significant role in advancing the understanding of nutritional needs and challenges faced by individuals with gastric cancer.KIM IH:Kim IH is a researcher and co-author of a study that compares various nutritional assessments in detecting malnutrition among gastric cancer patients. This study was published in the World Journal of Gastroenterology, highlighting Kim IH's involvement in important research aimed at improving the nutritional evaluation of individuals affected by gastric cancer.VELASCO C:Velasco C is a researcher who participated in a multicentre study on nutritional screening tools.GARCIA E:Garcia E is a researcher who co-authored a study on nutritional risk in hospitalized patients.RODRIGUEZ V:Rodriguez V is a researcher involved in the study comparing nutritional screening tools.FRIAS L:Frias L is a researcher who contributed to the multicentre study on nutritional risk.GARRIGA R:Garriga R is a researcher who co-authored the study on nutritional screening tools.ZHEN SUN:Zhen Sun is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on nutritional risk screening in postoperative outcomes.XIN ‚Äì JUAN KONG:Xin ‚Äì Juan Kong is a researcher who co-authored a systematic review on nutritional risk screening.XUE JING:Xue Jing is a researcher involved in the systematic review of nutritional risk screening.RUN ‚Äì JUN DENG:Run ‚Äì Jun Deng is a researcher who contributed to the systematic review on nutritional risk screening.ZI ‚Äì BIN TIAN:Zi ‚Äì Bin Tian is a researcher involved in the systematic review of nutritional risk screening.DA SILVA FINK J:Da Silva Fink J is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on subjective global assessment of nutritional status.DANIEL DE MELLO P:Daniel de Mello P is a researcher involved in the systematic review of nutritional status assessment.NORTH AMERICAN SURGICAL NUTRITION SUMMIT:The North American Surgical Nutrition Summit is a conference dedicated to discussing best practices and consensus recommendations for nutritional support in surgical patients. This event serves as a platform for healthcare professionals to share insights and establish guidelines aimed at improving the nutritional care of individuals undergoing surgery.THORELL A:Thorell A is a researcher who contributed to the guidelines for perioperative care in bariatric surgery.MACCORMICK AD:MacCormick AD is a researcher involved in the ERAS Society recommendations for bariatric surgery.AWAD S:Awad S is a researcher known for significant contributions to the field of bariatric surgery. He played a key role in developing guidelines for perioperative care, ensuring that patients receive optimal support before, during, and after their surgical procedures. Additionally, Awad S conducted studies on the protective effects of preoperative feeding, highlighting its importance in enhancing patient outcomes in bariatric surgery. His work reflects a commitment to improving surgical practices and patient care in this specialized area of medicine.MALTBY JR:Maltby JR is a researcher who has published on fasting and its implications in anesthesia.MENDLESON CL:Mendelson CL is a researcher known for his work on aspiration of stomach contents during obstetric anesthesia.HUTCHINSON A:Hutchinson A is a researcher who studied gastric fluid volume and pH in elective inpatients.HAUSEL J:Hausel J is a researcher who studied the effects of carbohydrate-rich drinks on preoperative discomfort.ZELIC M:Zelic M is a researcher who investigated the influence of preoperative oral feeding on stress response after colon cancer resection.VAN DEN BERGHE G:Van den Berghe G is a researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the field of intensive insulin therapy, particularly in critically ill patients. His work focuses on the implications of intensive insulin control for nutritional management, highlighting its relevance in improving patient outcomes in critical care settings.FINFER S:Finfer S is a researcher who studied glucose control in critically ill patients.LJUNGQVIST O:Ljungqvist O is a researcher who has published on preoperative carbohydrate loading and its effects.SMITH I:Smith I is a researcher who contributed to the literature on fasting and anesthesia.SUBJECTIVE GLOBAL ASSESSMENT:Subjective Global Assessment is a method used to evaluate nutritional status based on clinical judgment. This approach relies on the clinician's expertise to assess an individual's nutritional condition, integrating both subjective and objective data to form a comprehensive evaluation.EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF ANESTHESIOLOGY:The European Society of Anesthesiology provides guidelines for perioperative fasting in adults and children.ANN SURG:Annals of Surgery is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research related to surgical practices.J SURG RES:Journal of Surgical Research publishes articles related to surgical techniques and outcomes.J GASTROINTEST SURG:Journal of Gastrointestinal Surgery publishes research on surgical procedures related to the gastrointestinal tract.BALTIMORE:Baltimore is a city in Maryland, USA, where a multicenter prospective cohort study was conducted.BEIJING:Beijing is the capital city of China, where a multicenter prospective cohort study was conducted.PILAR MAT√çA MART√çN:Dr. Pilar Mat√≠a Mart√≠n is a medical professional specializing in the study of specific pathologies related to nutrition. She serves as an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid. Additionally, she holds the position of associate professor at Universidad Complutense in Madrid, where she contributes to the education and training of future medical professionals.TERESA RUIZ GRACIA:Dr. Teresa Ruiz Gracia is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid.FEDERICO MIGUEL CUESTA TRIANA:Dr. Federico Miguel Cuesta Triana is an attending physician in the Geriatrics Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid.NATALIA P√âREZ FERRE:Dr. Natalia P√©rez Ferre is a medical professional specializing in nutritional support for septic and critically ill patients. She serves as an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid, where she applies her expertise to enhance the care of patients requiring specialized nutritional interventions.RON PENSO ESPINOZA:Dr. Rona Penso Espinoza is a medical professional involved in nutritional support for septic and critically ill patients.CLARA MARCUELLO FONCILLAS:Clara Marcuello Foncillas is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid. She is a medical professional who specializes in providing nutritional support for burn and trauma patients, demonstrating her expertise in both endocrinology and nutrition within a clinical setting.PAULA FERN√ÅNDEZ MART√çNEZ:Dr. Paula Fern√°ndez Mart√≠nez is a dedicated medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. She is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with neurological diseases and is associated with the Secci√≥n de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario in Le√≥n. In her role, she contributes to the development of guidelines for artificial nutrition, demonstrating her commitment to improving patient care in her field.POSTOPERATIVE INSULIN RESISTANCE:Postoperative insulin resistance is a condition that may arise after surgery, potentially influenced by factors such as short-term starvation.MULTICENTER PROSPECTIVE COHORT STUDY:A multicenter prospective cohort study is a type of research design used to assess the impact of nutritional support on clinical outcomes.SHORT-TERM STARVATION:√ÅNGELA AMENGUAL GALBARTE:√Ångela Amengual Galbarte is a fourth-year resident physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid.POBLACI√ìN MAYOR:The older population, particularly those over 80 years old, is experiencing significant growth, impacting healthcare and society.HERTFORDSHIRE:Hertfordshire is a location where a cohort study on sarcopenia prevalence was conducted, involving elderly participants.ESTUDIO ELLI:The ELLI study is a multicentric Spanish study that assessed the prevalence of sarcopenia among non-institutionalized elderly individuals over 69 years old.FRADEA:The FRADEA study is a Spanish study that reported on the prevalence of frailty among elderly individuals.GENDER:Gender is a demographic factor that influences the prevalence of sarcopenia and frailty, with variations observed between men and women.PATEL ET AL.:Patel et al. are researchers who evaluated the prevalence of sarcopenia in a cohort study in Hertfordshire.LONGITUDINAL ENGLISH STUDY:The Longitudinal English Study on aging assessed the prevalence of frailty among older adults in England.MASAN√âS ET AL.:Masan√©s et al. conducted research in Spain to establish reference points for diagnosing sarcopenia using bioelectrical impedance analysis.DIAGN√ìSTICO DE SARCOPENIA:The diagnosis of sarcopenia involves criteria that assess muscle mass and physical function, which have evolved over time.FISIOPATOLOG√çA DE LA SARCOPENIA:The pathophysiology of sarcopenia includes various factors such as hormonal changes, inflammation, and aging that contribute to muscle loss.FACTORES DE ESTILO DE VIDA:EWGSOP:The European Working Group on Sarcopenia in Older People (EWGSOP) provides guidelines and criteria for diagnosing sarcopenia.IWG:The International Working Group on Sarcopenia (IWG) develops consensus definitions and diagnostic criteria for sarcopenia.SCWD:Sarcopenia, Cachexia and Wasting Disorders (SCWD) focuses on the study and management of muscle wasting conditions.WALKING SPEED:Walking speed is a functional measure used to assess mobility and physical performance in individuals, often evaluated in clinical settings.MUSCLE MASS:Muscle mass refers to the amount of muscle tissue in the body, which plays a crucial role in overall health and physical function. It can be significantly affected by various factors, including cancer and its treatments, which may lead to a decreased muscle mass and an increased need for nutritional support to help maintain or restore muscle tissue. Additionally, muscle mass can be evaluated using techniques such as Bioelectrical Impedance Analysis (BIA) and Dual-Energy X-ray Absorptiometry (DEXA), which provide insights into an individual's muscle composition and health status.KNEE EXTENSION:Knee extension is a physical test used to measure muscle strength in the lower body, relevant in assessing sarcopenia.AGE AGEING:Age Ageing is a journal that publishes research related to aging, including studies on sarcopenia and its implications for older adults.FUNCTIONAL STATUS:Functional status refers to an individual's ability to perform activities of daily living, which can be affected by sarcopenia and related conditions.CHRONIC OBSTRUCTIVE PULMONARY DISEASE:Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) is a progressive lung disease characterized by increasing breathlessness and breathing difficulties. It is primarily caused by long-term exposure to irritating gases or particulate matter, most commonly from cigarette smoke, as well as other harmful substances. COPD is often associated with bronchiectasis and can also be related to cystic fibrosis. The condition not only affects respiratory function but can also negatively impact muscle mass and strength, particularly in older adults. Additionally, individuals with COPD may require nutritional support to manage their health effectively.RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS:Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition that can contribute to muscle weakness and sarcopenia in older adults.FISIOPATOL√ìGIA DE LA FRAGILIDAD:La fisiopatolog√≠a de la fragilidad se refiere a los cambios biol√≥gicos y metab√≥licos que ocurren en el cuerpo, especialmente en los sistemas inmunol√≥gico, neuroendocrino y musculoesquel√©tico, que contribuyen a la fragilidad en los ancianos.FNT-Œë:El factor de necrosis tumoral alfa (FNT-Œ±) es una citoquina involucrada en la inflamaci√≥n y se ha asociado con la fragilidad y la sarcopenia.SISTEMA NEUROENDOCRINO:El sistema neuroendocrino es un sistema que regula las hormonas en el cuerpo y se ha relacionado con la aparici√≥n de fragilidad en el envejecimiento.SISTEMA MUSCULOESQUEL√âTICO:El sistema musculoesquel√©tico incluye m√∫sculos y huesos, y su deterioro est√° asociado con la fragilidad y la sarcopenia en los ancianos.FISICA:F√≠sica is a field of study that encompasses the principles of matter and energy, often related to health and physical conditions such as sarcopenia and frailty.CES-D:The Center for Epidemiologic Studies Depression Scale (CES-D) is a screening tool used to identify depressive symptoms in the general population.PATOLOGIAS ESPECIFICAS:Patolog√≠as espec√≠ficas refers to specific health conditions that may be diagnosed based on certain criteria, including frailty.INTERVENCION NUTRICIONAL:Intervenci√≥n nutricional refers to dietary interventions aimed at improving nutritional status, particularly in the elderly to combat frailty and sarcopenia.EJERCICIO FISICO:Ejercicio f√≠sico refers to physical exercise, which is an important component in the management and prevention of frailty and sarcopenia.MUSCULO:M√∫sculo refers to muscle tissue, which has a maximum storage limit for creatine. This tissue is influenced by supplementation, indicating that the amount of creatine that can be stored in muscle is finite and can be enhanced through dietary or supplemental means.FRAIL:Frail is a set of criteria used to evaluate the fragility of elderly individuals, focusing on their physical capabilities and health status.PRE-FRAGILITY:Pre-fragility refers to a state where individuals meet 1-2 criteria indicating they are at risk of becoming frail, highlighting the need for intervention.FRAGILITY:Fragility is a condition characterized by the presence of 3 or more criteria indicating a significant decline in physical health and increased dependency.GRUPO DE EXPERTOS DE ESPEN:El Grupo de Expertos de ESPEN es un grupo que proporciona directrices sobre la nutrici√≥n en pacientes, incluyendo ancianos.MUSCULATURA:MUSCULATURA refers to the muscle mass of the body, which is influenced by protein intake and physical activity. Muscle mass and strength are essential for maintaining physical independence, particularly in the elderly population.FRUCTOOLIGOSAC√ÅRIDOS:Fructooligosaccharides are prebiotic fibers that promote the growth of beneficial gut bacteria and have been shown to improve muscle strength in frail elderly individuals.ENSAYO CL√çNICO:The "ENSAYO CL√çNICO," or clinical trial, is a type of experimental study designed to evaluate the effects of specific interventions on health outcomes. These interventions can include medical treatments, dietary patterns, and supplements, particularly in populations such as the elderly. Clinical trials involve the assignment and control of a study factor to assess its impact on health, thereby contributing valuable data to the field of medical research.DEHIDROEPIANDROSTERONA:Dehidroepiandrosterona is a hormone studied for its effects on muscle mass and strength in postmenopausal women and men with low testosterone levels.TIBOLONA:Tibolone is a hormonal compound that has shown potential benefits in increasing grip strength and lean mass in postmenopausal women.OSTARINA:Ostarine is a selective androgen receptor modulator that has shown proven effects on muscle in animal models.MODULADORES SINT√âTICOS DE ANDR√ìGENOS:Synthetic androgen modulators are drugs being researched for their potential benefits in treating muscle-related conditions.INHIBIDORES DE LA ENZIMA CONVERTIDORA DE ANGIOTENSINA:ACE inhibitors are being studied for their effects on functional capacity and muscle strength.MIOSTATINA:Myostatin is a negative regulator of muscle mass, and its blockers are being researched for their potential to increase muscle growth.GINKGO BILOBA:Ginkgo biloba is a herbal supplement that is being researched for its effects on cognitive and physical function.COENZIMA Q:Coenzyme Q is a compound studied for its role in energy production and potential benefits for muscle health.NORTTESTOSTERONA:EXERCISE AEROBIC:Aerobic exercise includes activities like walking or cycling that improve cardiovascular fitness and overall health, recommended for the elderly.EXERCISE OF STRENGTH:Strength exercise involves resistance training to enhance muscle strength and combat sarcopenia, particularly important for older adults.EXERCISES OF BALANCE:Balance exercises are activities designed to improve stability and prevent falls in the elderly, such as tai chi and standing on one leg.EXERCISES OF FLEXIBILITY:Flexibility exercises aim to increase the range of motion in muscles and joints, which is important for maintaining mobility in older adults.ROME:Rome is a city known for its historical significance and is often associated with studies on aging and health issues, including sarcopenia and frailty in the elderly.UNITED NATIONS:The United Nations is an international organization that publishes reports on global issues, including population aging and health.HERTFORDSHIRE COHORT STUDY:The Hertfordshire Cohort Study investigates the prevalence of sarcopenia in community-dwelling older people in the UK.ELLI STUDY:The ELLI study investigates the prevalence of sarcopenia in patients attending outpatient geriatric clinics. It focuses on understanding how common this condition is among the elderly population receiving care in these settings.INTERNATIONAL SARCOPENIA INITIATIVE:The International Sarcopenia Initiative (EWGSOP and IWGS) conducts systematic reviews on sarcopenia in aging adults.ENGLISH LONGITUDINAL STUDY OF AGEING:The English Longitudinal Study of Ageing provides findings on the prevalence of frailty and disability among older adults.FRAILTY AND DEPENDENCE IN ALBACETE STUDY:The Frailty and Dependence in Albacete study assesses the prevalence of frailty in a Spanish elderly population.SURVEY OF HEALTH, AGEING AND RETIREMENT IN EUROPE:The SHARE study compares patterns of frailty in older adults across different income countries.STUDY ON GLOBAL AGEING AND ADULT HEALTH:The SAGE study focuses on global aging and health issues affecting older adults.AMERICAN JOURNAL OF EPIDEMIOLOGY:The American Journal of Epidemiology publishes studies on the epidemiology of sarcopenia among the elderly.JOURNAL OF NUTRITION HEALTH AND AGING:The Journal of Nutrition Health and Aging publishes research on the prevalence of sarcopenia in community-dwelling elderly.CLINICAL GERIATRIC MEDICINE:Clinical Geriatric Medicine discusses the pathogenesis and management of sarcopenia.ILSIRENTE STUDY:The ilSIRENTE study examines the relationship between sarcopenia and mortality risk in frail older persons aged 80 years and older.MATURITAS:Maturitas is a journal dedicated to publishing systematic reviews and research focused on aging and health. It encompasses a wide range of studies, including those related to nutritional supplementation and exercise in the elderly. Additionally, Maturitas specifically addresses the relationship between nutrition and frailty in older adults, contributing valuable insights to the field of gerontology.ARTAZA-ARTABE I:Artaza-Artabe I is a researcher who has conducted a review on the relationship between nutrition and frailty in the elderly.LANDI F:Landi F is a researcher who has contributed to studies on sarcopenia and its implications for older adults.SCHNEIDER SM:Schneider SM is a researcher who has worked on the prevalence and interventions for sarcopenia in aging adults.Z√ö√ëIGA C:Z√∫√±iga C is a researcher involved in the systematic review of sarcopenia in aging adults.ARAI H:Arai H is a researcher contributing to the understanding of sarcopenia in older adults.BOIRIE Y:Boirie Y is a researcher who has studied the prevalence of sarcopenia in aging adults.HARTTGEN K:Harttgen K is a researcher who has compared patterns of frailty in older adults across different income countries.KOWAL P:Kowal P is a researcher involved in studies on aging and health.STRULIK H:Strulik H is a researcher who has contributed to studies on frailty in older adults.CHATTERJI S:Chatterji S is a researcher involved in the Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe.VOLLMER S:Vollmer S is a researcher who has worked on aging and health studies.BAUMGARTNER RN:Baumgartner RN is a researcher who has studied the epidemiology of sarcopenia among the elderly.FIELDING RA:Fielding RA is a researcher who has contributed to the consensus definition of sarcopenia.MUSCARITOLI M:Muscaritoli M is a prominent author and researcher in the fields of nutrition and oncology. He has made significant contributions to the guidelines on enteral nutrition specifically tailored for oncology patients. Additionally, Muscaritoli M has played a crucial role in defining key concepts such as sarcopenia, cachexia, and pre-cachexia, which are critical in understanding the nutritional challenges faced by patients with chronic diseases. His research also explores the intricate relationship between sarcopenia and various chronic conditions. Furthermore, Muscaritoli M has contributed to the European Respiratory Society's statement on nutritional assessment and therapy in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), highlighting his commitment to improving nutritional care in respiratory illnesses.DHILLON RJS:Dhillon RJS is a researcher discussing the pathogenesis and management of sarcopenia.GARIBALLA S:Gariballa S is a researcher who has studied the prevalence and prognostic significance of sarcopenia in hospitalized patients.BIOLO G:Biolo G is a researcher who focuses on muscle dysfunction, particularly in relation to sarcopenia and chronic diseases.AGING CLIN EXP RES:Aging Clinical and Experimental Research is a journal that publishes studies on geriatric syndromes, including frailty and its predictors.FRONT AGING NEUROSCI:Frontiers in Aging Neuroscience is a journal that discusses the relationship between sarcopenia and physical frailty.AGEING RES REV:Ageing Research Reviews is a journal that reviews literature on frailty and aging, including modifications to frailty phenotype criteria.J NUTR HEALTH AGING:The Journal of Nutrition Health and Aging publishes studies on nutritional status and frailty in older persons.PROC NUTR SOC:Proceedings of the Nutrition Society publishes research on nutrition and physical activity for the prevention of age-related sarcopenia.CLIN INTERV AGING:Clinical Interventions in Aging is a journal that provides an overview of frailty syndrome and its implications for older adults.OBSERVATORY OF SARCOPENIA:The Observatory of Sarcopenia is a research initiative established by the Spanish Society of Geriatrics and Gerontology. Its primary focus is on the study and understanding of sarcopenia, a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength, particularly in older adults. The project aims to address the challenges posed by sarcopenia, enhancing knowledge and promoting strategies to mitigate its effects on the aging population.VAN KAN GA:Van Kan GA is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of frailty in older adults.ANKER SD:Anker SD is a researcher who has studied frailty and its relationship with chronic diseases.BAUER JM:Bauer JM is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.BERNABEI R:Bernabei R is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of frailty in older populations.TRACY RP:Tracy RP is a researcher involved in studies on inflammation and frailty.KOP WJ:Kop WJ is a researcher who has studied the relationship between frailty and chronic diseases.HIRSCH CH:Hirsch CH is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.LENG SX:Leng SX is a researcher who has studied the geriatric syndrome of frailty.CAPPOLA AR:Cappola AR is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and its predictors.ANDERSEN RE:Andersen RE is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of frailty in older adults.BLACKMAN MR:Blackman MR is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.KOENIG K:Koenig K is a researcher who has studied the relationship between frailty and chronic diseases.BLAIR M:Blair M is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.THEOU O:Theou O is a researcher who has studied modifications to frailty phenotype criteria.CANN L:Cann L is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.BLODGETT J:Blodgett J is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of frailty in older adults.WALLACE LM:Wallace LM is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.BROTHERS TD:Brothers TD is a researcher who has studied frailty and its implications for health.ABELLAN VAN KAN G:Abellan van Kan G is a researcher involved in the I.A.N.A. Task Force on frailty assessment.ROLLAND Y:Rolland Y is a researcher who has studied frailty and its implications for older adults.FAIRHALL N:Fairhall N is a researcher involved in studies on preventing frailty in older people.KURRLE SE:Kurrle SE is a researcher who has studied frailty and its prevention.SHERRINGTON C:Sherrington C is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and physical activity.LORD SR:Lord SR is a researcher who has studied the relationship between frailty and falls in older adults.LOCKWOOD K:Lockwood K is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.JOHN B:John B is a researcher who has contributed to studies on frailty and its prevention.BOLWEIN J:Bolwein J is a researcher involved in studies on nutritional status and frailty.DIEKMANN R:Diekmann R is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.KAISER MJ:Kaiser MJ is a researcher who has studied nutritional status and frailty.UTER W:Uter W is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.VIDAL K:Vidal K is a researcher who has studied the relationship between nutrition and frailty.CHEN X:Chen X is a researcher who has provided an overview of frailty syndrome.MAO G:Mao G is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and aging.DEER RR:Deer RR is a researcher who has studied protein intake and muscle function in older adults.VOLPI E:Volpi E is a researcher involved in studies on protein intake and its effects on aging.TRIANA FC:Triana FC is a researcher involved in studies on sarcopenia and aging.G√ìMEZ-CABRERA MC:G√≥mez-Cabrera MC is a researcher who has studied the role of sarcopenia in aging.L√ìPEZ-SOTO A:L√≥pez-Soto A is a researcher involved in studies on sarcopenia and its implications for health.MASAN√âS F:Masan√©s F is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of sarcopenia.MART√çN PM:Mart√≠n PM is a researcher involved in studies on sarcopenia and aging.CLIN NUT:SPANISH SOCIETY OF GERIATRICS AND GERONTOLOGY:A professional organization dedicated to the study and promotion of geriatrics and gerontology in Spain.ESPEN EXPERT GROUP:A group of experts providing recommendations on nutrition and exercise for optimal muscle function in aging individuals.MATURES:A journal that publishes research on aging and health, including studies on nutrition and physical activity.N-3 POLYUNSATURATED FATTY ACIDS:Essential fatty acids that are important for health, particularly in aging populations, and are often included in nutritional studies.HIGH-PROTEIN ORAL NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENTS:Supplements designed to provide additional protein to support muscle health in older adults, particularly those with sarcopenia.FC TRIANA:FC Triana is a researcher who co-authored studies related to sarcopenia and its implications in older adults.MC G√ìMEZ-CABRERA:MC G√≥mez-Cabrera is a researcher focused on the effects of nutrition and exercise on aging populations.A L√ìPEZ-SOTO:A L√≥pez-Soto is a researcher contributing to the understanding of sarcopenia and its treatment.F MASAN√âS:F Masan√©s is a researcher involved in studies related to sarcopenia and geriatric health.PM MART√çN:PM Mart√≠n is a researcher who has published work on sarcopenia and its impact on older adults.J BAUER:J Bauer is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of dietary protein intake in older adults.G BIOLO:G Biolo is a researcher focused on nutrition and its effects on muscle function in aging individuals.T CEDERHOLM:T Cederholm is a researcher involved in studies on nutrition and aging, particularly regarding protein intake.M CESARI:M Cesari is a researcher who has published work on the relationship between nutrition and sarcopenia.NEP DEUTZ:NEP Deutz is a researcher focused on protein intake and exercise for older adults.R BARAZZONI:R Barazzoni is a researcher involved in studies on nutrition and muscle health in aging populations.Y BOIRIE:Y Boirie is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of dietary needs in older adults.A BOSY-WESTPHAL:A Bosy-Westphal is a researcher focused on nutrition and its impact on health in older individuals.H BISCHOFF-FERRARI:H Bischoff-Ferrari is a researcher known for work on vitamin D and its role in fall prevention among older adults.B DAWSON-HUGHES:B Dawson-Hughes is a researcher who has studied the effects of vitamin D on health in aging populations.HB STAEHELIN:HB Staehelin is a researcher involved in studies on aging and health, particularly regarding fall prevention.JE ORAV:JE Orav is a researcher who has contributed to studies on health outcomes in older adults.AE STUCK:AE Stuck is a researcher focused on geriatric health and fall prevention strategies.R THEILER:R Theiler is a researcher involved in studies related to vitamin D and its health implications for older adults.A TICINESI:A Ticinesi is a researcher who has studied nutrition and inflammation in older individuals.T MESCHI:T Meschi is a researcher focused on the impact of nutrition on health in aging populations.F LAURETANI:F Lauretani is a researcher involved in studies on aging and nutrition.G FELIS:G Felis is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of nutrition in older adults.F FRANCHI:F Franchi is a researcher focused on the role of nutrition in aging and health.C PEDROLLI:C Pedrolli is a researcher involved in studies on dietary antioxidants and their effects on health in older adults.HL HUTCHINS-WIESE:HL Hutchins-Wiese is a researcher who has studied the impact of dietary supplements on physical performance in postmenopausal women.A KLEPPINGER:A Kleppinger is a researcher focused on nutrition and its effects on health in aging populations.K ANNIS:K Annis is a researcher involved in studies on dietary interventions for older adults.E LIVA:E Liva is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of nutrition in older individuals.CJ LAMMI-KEEFE:CJ Lammi-Keefe is a researcher focused on nutrition and its impact on health in aging populations.HA DURHAM:HA Durham is a researcher involved in studies on dietary interventions for older adults.JT DUNCAN:JT Duncan is a researcher who has studied the effects of probiotics and prebiotics on health in aging populations.HJ FLINT:HJ Flint is a researcher focused on the health benefits of probiotics and prebiotics in older adults.M YANNAKOULIA:M Yannakoulia is a researcher who has studied the relationship between frailty and nutrition in older individuals.E NTANASI:E Ntanasi is a researcher involved in studies on nutrition and aging.CA ANASTASIOU:CA Anastasiou is a researcher focused on the impact of nutrition on health in older adults.N SCARMEAS:N Scarmeas is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of frailty and nutrition in aging populations.DT VILLAREAL:DT Villareal is a researcher focused on the effects of weight loss and exercise on frailty in older adults.M BANKS:M Banks is a researcher involved in studies on frailty and nutrition in older individuals.DR SINACORE:DR Sinacore is a researcher who has studied the impact of exercise on frailty in older adults.C SIENER:C Siener is a researcher focused on the relationship between obesity, exercise, and frailty.S KLEIN:S Klein is a researcher involved in studies on nutrition and its effects on health in older adults.C BEAUDART:C Beaudart is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of nutrition and physical activity in the prevention of sarcopenia.A DAWSON:A Dawson is a researcher involved in studies on nutrition and its impact on aging populations.SC SHAW:SC Shaw is a researcher focused on the role of nutrition in the prevention and treatment of sarcopenia.NC HARVEY:NC Harvey is a researcher who has studied the relationship between nutrition and health in older adults.JA KANIS:JA Kanis is a researcher involved in studies on osteoporosis and its relationship with nutrition in aging populations.N BINKLEY:N Binkley is a researcher focused on the role of nutrition in the prevention of sarcopenia.A DE SPIEGELEER:A De Spiegeleer is a researcher involved in studies on the treatment of sarcopenia in clinical practice.M PETROVIC:M Petrovic is a researcher focused on the clinical management of sarcopenia.P BOECKXSTAENS:P Boeckxstaens is a researcher involved in studies on the treatment of sarcopenia.N VAN DEN NOORTGATE:N Van Den Noortgate is a researcher focused on the clinical aspects of sarcopeniaTERESA DE GRADO MANCHADO:Teresa de Grado Manchado is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Infanta Elena in Valdemoro, Madrid.RONA PENSO ESPINOZA:Rona Penso Espinoza is a fourth-year resident in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid.ALEJANDRA DUR√ÅN RODR√çGUEZ-HERVADA:Alejandra Dur√°n Rodr√≠guez-Hervada is an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl√≠nico San Carlos in Madrid.NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN CRITICAL PATIENTS:Nutritional support in critical patients is a medical approach discussed in recent years, focusing on the nutritional needs of critically ill patients.UNIDADES DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:Unidades de Cuidados Intensivos (ICUs) are specialized hospital departments designed to provide intensive care and monitoring for critically ill patients. Within these healthcare settings, catheter-related infections pose a significant concern, highlighting the critical nature of infection control in the management of patients in ICUs.DESNUTRICI√ìN CAL√ìRICO-PROTEICA:NUTRIC SCORE:The NUTRIC SCORE is a comprehensive scoring system designed to assess the nutritional risk of critically ill patients, particularly in critical care settings. It serves as a valuable tool for quantifying the risk of these patients developing adverse events and helps identify individuals who would benefit from optimized nutritional support. The NUTRIC Score utilizes an online calculator to evaluate various health parameters, providing a scoring system that indicates the risk of poor clinical outcomes. Additionally, it assesses the need for aggressive nutritional intervention, ensuring that healthcare providers can make informed decisions regarding nutritional care for critically ill patients. Overall, the NUTRIC SCORE is essential for improving patient outcomes through targeted nutritional assessment and intervention.HORMONAS CONTRARREGULADORAS:Counter-regulatory hormones are involved in the metabolic response to stress in critically ill patients.GLUC√ìGENOLISIS:Glycogenolysis is the process of breaking down glycogen to glucose, which is increased in critically ill patients.DISFUNCI√ìN MULTIORG√ÅNICA:Multi-organ dysfunction is a serious condition that can occur in critically ill patients, leading to increased mortality.TIEMPO DE HOSPITALIZACI√ìN:Length of hospitalization is often prolonged in critically ill patients due to complications and recovery needs.DA√ëO OXIDATIVO CELULAR:Cellular oxidative damage can occur in critically ill patients and is a factor in their overall health status.VALORACI√ìN NUTRICIONAL COMPLETA:A complete nutritional assessment is essential for critically ill patients to determine their nutritional needs.EVALUACI√ìN DE LA FUNCI√ìN MUSCULAR:Assessment of muscle function is important for understanding the health status of critically ill patients.CANADIAN SOCIETY FOR CLINICAL NUTRITION:The Canadian Society for Clinical Nutrition (CSCN) offers guidelines regarding nutritional practices and recommendations for critically ill patients.CRITICAL CARE:Critical Care is both a medical specialty and a journal dedicated to the management and treatment of critically ill patients. As a medical specialty, Critical Care focuses on the diagnosis and management of life-threatening conditions, which may include situations that require parenteral nutrition. The term also encompasses the specialized care provided to patients facing such severe health challenges, often necessitating intensive monitoring and treatment. The journal serves as a platform for publishing research that advances the understanding and practices related to the care of these critically ill individuals.PACIENTE CR√çTICO:The entity "PACIENTE CR√çTICO" refers to a critically ill patient who is in a life-threatening condition and requires intensive medical care and close monitoring. Such patients often need specialized nutritional support, which may include parenteral nutrition. Additionally, they can benefit from immunomodulatory formulas to aid in their recovery. Overall, a paciente cr√≠tico is characterized by their severe health status, necessitating comprehensive medical attention and tailored nutritional interventions.CSCN:CSCN, or the Canadian Society for Clinical Nutrition, is a Canadian organization dedicated to providing clinical guidelines for nutrition in critically ill patients. The society emphasizes the importance of enteral nutrition over parenteral nutrition for this patient population, advocating for practices that enhance patient care and recovery through appropriate nutritional support.GASTO CAL√ìRICO:Caloric expenditure refers to the total number of calories burned by a patient, which is crucial for determining nutritional needs.CHOBAN P:Choban P is one of the authors of the ASPEN Clinical Guidelines for nutrition support.DICKERSON R:Dickerson R is one of the authors of the ASPEN Clinical Guidelines for nutrition support.MALONE A:Malone A is one of the authors of the ASPEN Clinical Guidelines for nutrition support.WORTHINGTON P:Worthington P is one of the authors of the ASPEN Clinical Guidelines for nutrition support.HEMODYNAMIC STABILITY:Hemodynamic stability refers to the stable condition of a patient's blood circulation, which is crucial before initiating nutritional support.MICROCIRCULATION:Microcirculation involves the flow of blood through the smallest blood vessels, which can be compromised in critically ill patients.SONDA PRE- O POSTPIL√ìRICA:Sonda pre- o postpil√≥rica refers to feeding tubes placed before or after the pylorus in the stomach, used in critical care settings.PACIENTES CR√çTICOS:"PACIENTES CR√çTICOS" refers to individuals in severe medical conditions who require intensive medical care and specialized nutritional interventions. These patients often face complications such as intestinal microcirculation damage and may experience conditions like hypoalbuminemia due to dilution. As a result, they necessitate careful evaluation of their nutritional status and may require parenteral nutrition to support their health. Overall, "PACIENTES CR√çTICOS" are characterized by their need for close monitoring and tailored medical attention to address their compromised health.F√ÅRMACOS VASOPRESORES:Los f√°rmacos vasopresores son medicamentos utilizados para aumentar la presi√≥n arterial en pacientes hipotensos, y su uso debe ser monitoreado durante la nutrici√≥n enteral.ATROFIA DE LA MUCOSA G√ÅSTRICA:La atrofia de la mucosa g√°strica es una condici√≥n que puede prevenirse mediante la administraci√≥n adecuada de nutrici√≥n enteral en pacientes cr√≠ticos.SIGNOS DE ISQUEMIA:Los signos de isquemia incluyen distensi√≥n abdominal, cantidad de residuo g√°strico y presencia de acidosis metab√≥lica, que deben ser vigilados en pacientes que reciben nutrici√≥n enteral.MICROCIRCULACI√ìN INTESTINAL:SEPSIS SEVERA:SEPSIS SEVERA is a severe condition characterized by a life-threatening response to infection, which leads to injury of the body's own tissues and organs. This condition was included as part of the study criteria for patients who were receiving various nutritional support methods. The severity of sepsis underscores its critical nature in clinical settings, highlighting the importance of effective management and intervention strategies.F√ìRMULA DE NE:Formula de NE refers to the specific nutritional formulas used in enteral nutrition for patients, tailored to their medical needs.CANADIAN GUIDELINES:The Canadian guidelines provide recommendations for nutritional support in critically ill patients, particularly regarding the use of specific formulas and supplements in patients with sepsis and other critical conditions.CRITICAL PATIENT:A critical patient is an individual who is in a life-threatening condition that necessitates intensive medical care and monitoring. These patients often require specialized nutritional support as part of their treatment. The care provided to critical patients is crucial due to the severity of their health status, highlighting the need for comprehensive medical attention.GLN:Glutamine (Gln) is another amino acid discussed in the context of nutritional support for critically ill patients, but its supplementation is not recommended due to lack of demonstrated benefits.FIBER ENRICHED FORMULAS:Fiber enriched formulas are nutritional preparations that include fiber to aid in digestion and nutrient absorption, but their routine use is not recommended in critical patients.PEPTIDIC FORMULAS:Peptidic formulas are specialized nutritional preparations that may be considered for patients with malabsorption or poor response to standard fiber formulas.BIFIDOBACTERIA:Bifidobacteria are beneficial bacteria that are stimulated by prebiotic fibers and are important for gut health, particularly in critically ill patients.ARG:Arginine (Arg) is recognized as a conditionally essential amino acid, particularly in the context of burned patients. Its significance lies in its role in promoting wound healing and facilitating the production of nitric oxide, which is crucial for various physiological processes.NUTRIC:NUTRIC is a scoring system used to assess the risk of malnutrition in patients.NICE SUGAR STUDY:The NICE SUGAR study is a multicenter trial that observed increased mortality in the intensive control group for blood glucose levels in critically ill patients.VAN DEN BERGHE:Van den Berghe is a researcher whose work demonstrated the benefits of strict glycemic control in critically ill patients.ICU:ICU refers to the Intensive Care Unit where critically ill patients receive specialized care.ENERGY:ALCOH√ìLICOS:Alcoholics are identified as patients at risk of thiamine deficiency in critical care settings.MALNUTRIDOS:Malnourished patients are at risk of thiamine deficiency and require careful monitoring in critical care.ASPEN 7:ASPEN 7 provides guidelines for nutrition in special situations, particularly in critical care settings.INSUFICIENCIA HEPATICA:Insuficiencia hep√°tica involves liver failure, where nutritional support is crucial to reduce infections and metabolic complications.PANCREATITIS AGUDA GRAVE:Pancreatitis aguda grave is a severe form of pancreatitis requiring early enteral nutrition to improve patient outcomes.TERAPIA DE REEMPLAZO RENAL CONTINUA:Continuous renal replacement therapy is a method for managing patients with acute renal failure, necessitating specific nutritional needs.KREYMANN:Kreymann is an author of the ESPEN guidelines on Enteral Nutrition in intensive care, contributing to the field of critical care nutrition.BURNHAM:Burnham is an author who has researched myopathies in critical illness and their nutritional aspects.ZIEGLER:Ziegler is an author known for his work on parenteral nutrition in critically ill patients.WILLMORE:Willmore is an author who has written about strategies for enhancing recovery in catabolic illness.BONGERS:Bongers is an author who has studied exogenous glutamine and its clinical evidence in critical care.CREE:Cree is an author who has researched postburn trauma insulin resistance and fat metabolism.MCCLAVE:McClave is an author involved in guidelines for nutrition support therapy in critically ill patients.MOURTZAKIS:Mourtzakis is an author who has worked on bedside ultrasound measurement of skeletal muscle in clinical nutrition.BARACOS:Baracos is an author who has studied clinical outcomes related to muscle mass in cancer and catabolic illnesses.CRITICAL CARE NUTRITION:Critical Care Nutrition is a guideline organization dedicated to providing recommendations and clinical practice guidelines for nutritional support in critically ill patients. It focuses on optimizing nutrition in critical care settings to enhance patient outcomes and improve recovery processes.NUTRITION SUPPORT THERAPY:Nutrition Support Therapy refers to the clinical practice of providing nutritional support to critically ill patients. It encompasses the methods and practices used to deliver nutritional support to patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through oral intake. This therapy is essential for ensuring that patients receive adequate nutrition during their recovery process, particularly when they are unable to consume food normally.RECOMENDACIONES SEMICYUC:Recomendaciones SEMICYUC are guidelines developed by the SEMICYUC for nutritional support in critically ill patients.GU√çAS ESPEN:Gu√≠as ESPEN are guidelines provided by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism regarding nutritional support in clinical settings.JPEN JOURNAL OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The JPEN Journal of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition is a scholarly journal dedicated to publishing research focused on nutrition support within clinical settings. It specifically addresses practices and protocols related to both parenteral and enteral nutrition, providing a platform for the dissemination of knowledge and advancements in the field of nutritional support.INTENSIVE CARE MEDICINE:Intensive Care Medicine is a peer-reviewed journal that publishes research on intensive care practices and outcomes.CANADIAN CRITICAL CARE CLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES COMMITTEE:The Canadian Critical Care Clinical Practice Guidelines Committee develops guidelines for nutrition support in critically ill patients.TAYLOR SJ:Taylor SJ is a researcher involved in trials assessing the effects of early enhanced enteral nutrition in head injury patients.IBRAHIM EH:Ibrahim EH is a researcher who studied the effects of early versus late enteral feeding in mechanically ventilated patients.DOIG GS:Doig GS is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on early enteral nutrition in critically ill patients.MUTLU GM:Mutlu GM is a researcher focused on gastrointestinal complications in patients on mechanical ventilation.KOZAR RA:Kozar RA is a researcher who studied enteral tolerance post-injury through standardized protocols.DAVIES AR:Davies AR is a researcher involved in a multicenter trial comparing nasojejunal and nasogastric nutrition in critical illness.PARENTERAL FEEDING:Parenteral feeding is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract, typically used when enteral feeding is not possible.SEPTIC MORBIDITY:Septic morbidity refers to complications arising from infections that can occur in patients, particularly those with abdominal trauma.MECHANICALLY VENTILATED PATIENTS:Mechanically ventilated patients are individuals who require assistance with breathing through mechanical ventilation, often in critical care settings.GASTRIC FEEDING:Gastric feeding is a method of enteral nutrition where food is delivered directly into the stomach.POST-PYLORIC FEEDING:Post-pyloric feeding is a method of enteral nutrition where food is delivered beyond the stomach, into the small intestine.IMMUNONUTRITION:Immunonutrition is a specialized nutritional approach designed to enhance the immune response, particularly in patients undergoing surgery for cancer, those suffering from trauma, and critically ill individuals. This field of study focuses on the effects of specific nutrients on the immune system, aiming to improve outcomes for patients in critical conditions. By implementing targeted nutritional strategies, immunonutrition seeks to bolster the immune system's effectiveness, thereby supporting recovery and overall health in vulnerable populations.ASPIRATION IN CRITICALLY ILL PATIENTS:Aspiration in critically ill patients refers to the inhalation of food, liquid, or vomit into the lungs, which can lead to serious complications.INSTITUTO DE INVESTIGACI√ìN BIOM√âDICA DE M√ÅLAGA:The Instituto de Investigaci√≥n Biom√©dica de M√°laga is a prominent research institute dedicated to biomedical studies and advancements in healthcare. It is particularly associated with the work of Gabriel Olveira Fuster, who specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. The institute plays a significant role in advancing research in these fields, contributing to the overall improvement of health outcomes through its focused studies and innovative approaches.VICTORIA CONTRERAS BOL√çVAR:Victoria Contreras Bol√≠var is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, currently practicing at the UGC de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n, which is part of the Hospital Regional Universitario de M√°laga. She is recognized for her expertise in the field, contributing to the healthcare services provided within the UGC of Endocrinology and Nutrition.PULMONARY DISEASE:Pulmonary disease encompasses various conditions affecting the lungs, including chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), bronchiectasis, and cystic fibrosis, which may require specialized nutritional support.CRITICAL ILLNESS:CASILDA OLVEIRA FUSTER:Casilda Olveira Fuster is a specialist in Pulmonology at the UGC de Neumolog√≠a y Cirug√≠a Tor√°cica, Hospital Regional Universitario de M√°laga, and the University of M√°laga.UNIVERSIDAD DE M√ÅLAGA:The Universidad de M√°laga is an educational institution where Casilda Olveira Fuster is affiliated.BRONQUIECTASIAS:Bronchiectasis, or bronquiectasias, is a medical condition characterized by the abnormal and permanent dilation of the bronchi. This dilation leads to a buildup of mucus, which significantly increases the risk of chronic respiratory infections and other complications. The condition often arises from infections or other lung diseases, and it is associated with chronic inflammation of the airways. As a result, individuals with bronchiectasis may experience not only respiratory issues but also nutritional deficiencies due to the impact on overall health.UGC DE ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN:UGC de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n is a clinical unit specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at the Hospital Regional Universitario de M√°laga.UGC DE NEUMOLOG√çA Y CIRUG√çA TOR√ÅCICA:UGC de Neumolog√≠a y Cirug√≠a Tor√°cica is a clinical unit specializing in pulmonology and thoracic surgery at the Hospital Regional Universitario de M√°laga.RTFQ:RTFQ refers to a gene that codes for a protein functioning as a chloride channel. This protein plays a crucial role in maintaining the balance of salt and water in various tissues, particularly in the respiratory and digestive systems. Mutations in the RTFQ gene can lead to significant health issues, notably in individuals with cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder that severely impacts lung function and digestive health. To address these challenges, specific medications are being developed to restore the function of the RTFQ protein, offering hope for improved health outcomes for patients affected by cystic fibrosis.EPOC:EPOC, or Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD), is a progressive lung disease characterized by obstructive ventilatory disorders that lead to increasing breathlessness and significant difficulties in breathing. This condition is often linked to long-term exposure to irritating gases or particulate matter, particularly from cigarette smoke, as well as various environmental factors. EPOC affects a large portion of the population, especially older adults, and is associated with systemic manifestations that can impact overall health.

Patients with EPOC may experience significant nutritional issues, necessitating dietary evaluations and monitoring of muscle function. The disease can also lead to complications such as the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), which can affect treatment duration. Due to its progressive nature, EPOC requires regular monitoring and treatment to manage symptoms and improve quality of life. Overall, EPOC is a serious condition that poses considerable morbidity and mortality risks, highlighting the importance of awareness and management strategies for those affected.IBERPOC:IBERPOC is a comprehensive study focused on Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) in Spain. It has identified the prevalence of COPD, which affects a significant portion of the adult population. Additionally, the study explores various aspects of the disease, providing valuable insights into its impact on the population.INSUFICIENCIA PANCREATICA:Pancreatic insufficiency is a condition often associated with certain classes of RTFQ gene mutations.PAIS VASCO:EPI-SCAN:EPI-SCAN is a study that reported a global prevalence of COPD in Spain, highlighting the impact of the disease on public health.CEUTA:Ceuta is a city in Spain noted for having one of the highest mortality rates for COPD among women.NEUMOLOGIA:Neumolog√≠a refers to the field of medicine that deals with respiratory diseases, including COPD.MUTATION CLASSIFICATION:Mutation classification refers to the categorization of genetic mutations that can impact diseases like cystic fibrosis, which may relate to respiratory conditions.MORBIDIDAD:Morbidity refers to the incidence of disease, which is notably high for COPD in Spain, causing significant health concerns.EDUCACI√ìN:Education level is identified as a significant risk factor for the prevalence of COPD, impacting diagnosis and treatment.TABACCO:FEV1:FEV1, or Volumen Espiratorio Forzado en el primer segundo, is a critical measure utilized to evaluate lung function in patients diagnosed with EPOC (Enfermedad Pulmonar Obstructiva Cr√≥nica). This metric assesses the volume of air that can be forcibly exhaled in the first second of a breath, providing essential insights into the respiratory health of individuals suffering from this chronic condition.ACTIVIDAD F√çSICA HABITUAL:La actividad f√≠sica habitual es un factor que puede influir en la calidad de vida y el pron√≥stico de los pacientes con EPOC.DISNEA:La disnea es un s√≠ntoma com√∫n en pacientes con EPOC, caracterizado por la dificultad para respirar.DETERIORO DE LA FUNCI√ìN PULMONAR:El deterioro de la funci√≥n pulmonar es un indicador clave en la progresi√≥n de la EPOC y su manejo cl√≠nico.ATRAPAMIENTO A√âREO:El atrapamiento a√©reo es un fen√≥meno que ocurre en la EPOC, donde el aire queda atrapado en los pulmones, dificultando la respiraci√≥n.ALTERACIONES GASOM√âTRICAS:Las alteraciones gasom√©tricas son cambios en los niveles de gases en la sangre que pueden ocurrir en pacientes con EPOC.HIPERTENSI√ìN PULMONAR:La hipertensi√≥n pulmonar es una complicaci√≥n que puede desarrollarse en pacientes con EPOC, afectando su pron√≥stico.EXACERBACIONES:Las exacerbaciones son episodios agudos de empeoramiento de los s√≠ntomas en pacientes con EPOC, que pueden requerir atenci√≥n m√©dica.INGRESOS HOSPITALARIOS:Los ingresos hospitalarios son una medida de la gravedad de la EPOC y su impacto en la salud del paciente.CIRROSIS BILIAR FOCAL:Focal biliary cirrhosis is a liver condition that can develop in patients with cystic fibrosis, characterized by damage to the bile ducts.ALTERACIONES DEL METABOLISMO HIDROCARBONADO:Alterations in carbohydrate metabolism are common in cystic fibrosis patients, leading to complications such as diabetes.DIABETES RELACIONADA CON LA FQ:Diabetes related to cystic fibrosis is a common complication that increases with age among affected individuals.√çLEO MECONIAL:√çLEO MECONIAL refers to a medical condition known as meconium ileus, which occurs in approximately 5% of patients with cystic fibrosis. This condition is characterized by intestinal obstruction at birth due to the blockage of the intestines by thick meconium. As a result, affected newborns require prompt medical treatment to address the obstruction and manage the associated complications.ALFA-1-ANTITRIPSINA:ALFA-1-ANTITRIPSINA, also known as alpha-1-antitrypsin, is a protein that plays a critical role in protecting the lungs. It is particularly relevant in the context of various pulmonary diseases. A deficiency in this protein can lead to serious lung conditions, such as emphysema, and it is commonly tested in patients who present with respiratory symptoms.PACIENTE FUMADOR:A smoker patient with respiratory symptoms who may be at risk for developing EPOC and other lung diseases.S√çNDROME DE DESNUTRICI√ìN:Malnutrition syndrome refers to a range of conditions resulting from inadequate intake of nutrients, which is prevalent in patients with chronic diseases such as cystic fibrosis and EPOC.S√çNTOMAS RESPIRATORIOS:Respiratory symptoms include a range of issues such as shortness of breath, wheezing, and chronic cough, which are common in patients with EPOC and other lung diseases.BRONQUIECTASIS:SEPAR-ALAT:SEPAR-ALAT is a clinical guide organization focused on the diagnosis and treatment of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC).ALIMENTARY REFLUX:Alimentary reflux is a condition that can cause esophagitis and is mentioned as a complication affecting oral intake in patients with cystic fibrosis.COLOPAT√çA FIBROSANTE:Colopat√≠a fibrosante is a gastrointestinal complication associated with cystic fibrosis that can affect nutritional intake.ENFERMEDAD HEP√ÅTICA AVANZADA:Enfermedad hep√°tica avanzada is a severe liver condition that can impact the nutritional status of patients with cystic fibrosis.EUROPEAN RESPIRATORY SOCIETY:The European Respiratory Society is a professional organization dedicated to promoting lung health and advancing research in respiratory medicine. It focuses on various aspects of respiratory health, including chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and cystic fibrosis. The Society is known for publishing guidelines that aid in the diagnosis and management of respiratory diseases, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest research and best practices in the field. Through its efforts, the European Respiratory Society plays a crucial role in enhancing the understanding and treatment of respiratory conditions.OLVEIRA C ET AL.:Olveira C et al. conducted research on the relationship between nutritional status and pulmonary function in patients with cystic fibrosis.SOLER ET AL.:Soler et al. studied the prevalence of malnutrition in patients with EPOC and its impact on health outcomes.D√âFICIT ALFA-1-ANTITRIPSINA:Deficit alfa-1-antitripsina is a genetic condition that can lead to lung disease and is associated with nutritional challenges in affected individuals.OBSTRUCCI√ìN BRONQUIAL:Obstrucci√≥n bronquial refers to bronchial obstruction, which can cause significant respiratory issues and is relevant in the context of nutritional status in patients.INFARTO PULMONAR POR TEP:Infarto pulmonar por TEP refers to pulmonary infarction due to pulmonary embolism, a serious condition that can affect respiratory function and nutritional status.S√çNDROME DE YOUNG:S√≠ndrome de Young is a rare genetic disorder that can affect lung function and nutritional health.S√çNDROME DE U√ëAS AMARILLAS:S√≠ndrome de u√±as amarillas is a condition characterized by yellow nails and can be associated with respiratory diseases and nutritional deficiencies.RINOSINUSITIS PURULENTA:Rinosinusitis purulenta is a severe form of sinusitis that can impact respiratory health and nutritional status.PANBRONQUIOLITIS:Panbronquiolitis is a chronic inflammatory lung disease that can lead to respiratory complications and nutritional issues.QUISTE HIDAT√çDICO:Quiste hidat√≠dico is a parasitic infection that can affect the lungs